                <pb facs="0370" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2220c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-19T19:00:00-05:00">October 19, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>104. The Department has not received as yet from the French Government the
                    notification regarding the action taken concerning notes to China and Japan to
                    call their attention to obligations under the Kellogg Pact. The American note is
                    being withheld pending receipt of such notification. Kindly bring this to
                    Briand’s attention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
